"""Additional reviewed Kanto objects; separate append-only catalogue module."""
ROWS=[]
def add(key,label,subject,lines):
    replies=[s.strip() for s in lines.split('|')]
    assert len(replies)==11,(key,len(replies))
    ROWS.append(dict(key='kanto_object_extra_'+key,labels=[label],subject=subject,replies=replies))

add('founder_fuji','CinnabarIsland_PokemonLab_Entrance_Text_PhotoOfLabFounderDrFuji','The laboratory founder photograph identifies Dr. Fuji.',
"Mr. Fuji helped start this place? He has more chapters than I knew.|The founder's photograph connects his name to this laboratory. That is a useful fact, not his whole history.|So he helped build this place. There is a lot we have not asked him.|I know him through what he does now. This is a much earlier verse.|People can spend years building something before we ever learn their name.|We have found an earlier chapter with a surprisingly familiar face.|A familiar face in an unfamiliar part of his life.|Founding a laboratory takes more than knowing how to use one. Interesting background.|Some roots run farther than the branches we first notice.|Imagine every person we meet having a whole life we have barely opened.|I would like to know who took this picture and what the lab looked like that day.")
add('amber_pipe','CinnabarIsland_PokemonLab_ResearchRoom_Text_AnAmberPipe','An amber pipe is displayed in the research room.',
"Very pretty. Also not something I should test by blowing into it.|Amber used as a crafted object rather than a specimen. I wonder about its provenance.|Look with your eyes. It is still somebody else's property.|I expected notes and equipment. This feels like a personal detail.|That has the look of something whose owner knows exactly where it belongs.|One small object can make a room belong to a person rather than a profession.|An old material given a very particular purpose.|Interesting material choice. I would ask before making assumptions about its use.|A little piece of resin with another life folded around it.|It is a distinctive thing to keep in a research room. Someone chose it.|The small objects people keep often tell a different story from the plaques.")
add('bird_email','CinnabarIsland_PokemonLab_ResearchRoom_Text_LegendaryBirdEmail','Researchers name three legendary birds, admit their locations are unknown and plan to explore the cavern near Cerulean.',
"They wrote down what they do not know. That feels like a good start for an adventure.|The message separates known names from unknown locations. Their Cerulean expedition is a plan, not a confirmed sighting.|Three birds. No confirmed locations. Do not turn that into a promise about the cavern.|There is something exciting about a message that ends with people deciding to go look.|We would need supplies for an expedition, not just enthusiasm and a very impressive bird list.|A lead, three legends and a great deal left to discover. An excellent opening, provided we pack.|The unknown is doing quite a lot of work in that message.|Their next step is field observation. Good. A theory needs something to push back against it.|Three names, and the world still keeping their whereabouts to itself.|I appreciate a report that does not pretend a guess is a discovery.|I want to see what their field notes say when they return. Especially what surprised them.")
add('tectonix_grave','FiveIsland_MemorialPillar_Text_HereLiesTectonix','A carefully arranged stone cairn bears Tectonix name.',
"They took time to place every stone. We can take a little time to be quiet.|The careful arrangement says this place is tended. We should respect it.|Mind where you step. This matters to someone.|We do not have to fill this silence.|A name, a place, and somebody making sure neither is forgotten.|We arrived at the edge of somebody else's grief. We should enter gently.|A name kept above ground by patient hands.|Leave the cairn exactly as we found it.|The stones are doing the work of remembering. Let them.|There is no clever thing we need to say here.|I can remember this place without taking anything from its quiet.")
add('tectonix_offering','FiveIsland_MemorialPillar_Text_HereLiesTectonixLemonadeOffering','A can of lemonade has been left at Tectonix grave.',
"Somebody remembered a favorite drink. That is a very particular kind of love.|The offering preserves a personal detail. Remembering someone can be that specific.|Leave the can there. It belongs to this moment.|A favorite drink can say more than a grand speech.|Knowing what someone liked to drink means you shared ordinary days with them.|The smallest detail here makes the name feel like someone who was known.|An ordinary can, carrying more than it was made to hold.|We should not tidy away something that was deliberately left.|A little sweetness offered across a distance no road can cross.|It is such a familiar way to care for somebody. That is what makes it hurt.|I hope whoever left it knows the gesture can matter even without an audience.")
add('warehouse_penned','FiveIsland_RocketWarehouse_Text_ManyMonsLockedInPen','Many Pokemon are confined in a warehouse pen.',
"They should not have to wait in here wondering what happens next.|Confinement in this warehouse is a welfare concern. We should look for a safe way to release them.|Find the lock. Stay alert for anyone guarding it.|They are living creatures. The room is treating them like stock.|We need to help them, not stand here deciding how awful this is.|Somebody has mistaken a collection of lives for an inventory.|A room full of reasons to stop being patient with Rocket.|Assess the door and the surroundings. Opening it safely is the priority.|No creature belongs in a cage simply because someone found a buyer.|Let us be useful to them. They do not need us to make a speech.|I want the next thing they see outside that pen to be a safe way out.")
add('warehouse_empty','FiveIsland_RocketWarehouse_Text_PenUnlockedMonsFled','The pen is unlocked and the Pokemon appear to have escaped.',
"Empty in the best possible way. I hope they found somewhere safe.|The open door and empty pen indicate they left. Their safety beyond it is still unknown.|Good. Keep the exit clear in case any come back.|For once, an empty room is the hopeful part.|No one left inside. That is a relief worth taking a breath for.|An absence with a much better story behind it.|The cage has finally become a useless piece of furniture.|Door unlocked, occupants gone. Do not secure it again.|The room has lost its prisoners. May the paths outside be kinder.|I am glad there is nobody here for us to worry at through the bars.|I wish we could see where they went. For now, having left is enough.")
add('magnetic_report','FiveIsland_RocketWarehouse_Text_ReportWithGraphsAndText','A technical report concerns magnetic waves and Pokemon evolution; the player cannot understand it.',
"I recognize the words separately. Together they have formed a very tall fence.|The title concerns magnetic waves and evolution. We should not claim to understand methods we have not evaluated.|We cannot read enough of it to know what they did. Remember where it is.|It is unsettling to find careful work in a place used so carelessly.|A complicated report is not proof that the people using it have good intentions.|An impressive stack of graphs can still belong to a terrible enterprise.|The graphs are very tidy. That makes the rest of this place no better.|Technical detail requires review. The title alone cannot establish a result.|A difficult page does not become wise merely because we cannot read it.|I refuse to let a graph make me forget the pen in the next part of this warehouse.|Someone who understands the subject should examine this. We should preserve the evidence.")
add('warden_fossils','FuchsiaCity_WardensHouse_Text_MonPhotosFossilsOnDisplay','Pokemon photographs and fossils are displayed together in the wardens house.',
"Somebody has been collecting reasons to be amazed for a very long time.|Living observations and ancient remains, side by side. A nice reminder of the timescale involved.|A careful collection. Leave it that way.|There are so many different kinds of memory in one display.|I like a house that makes room for things its owner cares about.|A personal collection with a much larger world behind every piece.|Life, held still in two very different ways.|Photographs preserve appearances; fossils preserve physical traces. Useful companions.|A wall where recent days and very old years can sit together.|This feels collected with interest rather than arranged to impress visitors.|I would love to hear the story behind the oldest photograph here.")
add('warden_merch','FuchsiaCity_WardensHouse_Text_OldMonMerchandiseOnDisplay','Old Pokemon merchandise is kept on display.',
"Somebody kept their favorites. Even the slightly wobbly-looking ones.|Age alone does not explain why these were kept. Personal attachment often does.|If it matters to the owner, it does not need to impress us.|I like things that stayed loved after they stopped being new.|You can tell a lot about a kitchen from the mug nobody will replace. This feels similar.|A modest museum of things that once made somebody happy.|Yesterday's little treasures, spared the indignity of being thrown away.|Older designs can be interesting. So can the reasons someone preserves them.|A shelf can be an anchor for a younger version of yourself.|I would absolutely keep something ridiculous for sentimental reasons. I have no defense.|The wear is part of the story. I hope nobody tries to make everything look new.")
add('magazine_entry','LavenderTown_VolunteerPokemonHouse_Text_GrandPrizeDrawingClipped','The magazine prize drawing application has already been clipped out.',
"Somebody has already sent their little rectangle of hope.|The missing form suggests an entry was submitted. It tells us nothing about the result.|Someone beat us to the form. Good luck to them.|I hope waiting for the answer gives them something nice to look forward to.|No form left. We can at least avoid spilling anything on the rest of the magazine.|A tiny subplot has departed through the post.|A neat little hole where somebody put their optimism.|Application removed. Looking through the remaining pages will not produce another one.|A small wish has left this shelf and gone traveling.|Whoever clipped it out was very ready to win. I respect the enthusiasm.|I wonder whether they chose carefully or filled it in the moment they saw it.")
add('zubat_warning','MtMoon_1F_Text_ZubatIsABloodsucker','A Mt Moon sign warns visitors that Zubat feeds on blood.',
"Useful warning. I would prefer to remain an unsuitable snack.|A feeding adaptation, described with considerably more alarm than context.|Stay aware of the Zubat. No need to frighten every one we see.|That sign is not doing much for their public image.|We are not on the menu. Let us keep it that way without bothering them.|A factual warning delivered like a poster for a very small horror film.|The cave has posted its dietary preferences.|Know the local wildlife and avoid unnecessary contact. Straightforward advice.|A cave creature being a cave creature. We are the visitors.|Imagine your entire introduction to strangers being the least flattering thing about lunch.|I would like to learn how they live here, from a sensible distance.")
